== Looter ==
{{Enemy Infobox|Looter}}
{{Keyword Infobox|Thievery}}
'''Looter''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up in [[Act 1]] and [[Act 2]].

=== Pattern ===
{{Intents|Looter}}
* Uses {{Int|Looter|Mug}} for the first 2 turns.
* Has a 50% chance to use {{Int|Looter|Lunge}} or 50% chance to use {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}}.
** If {{Int|Looter|Lunge}} is used on its third turn, it will then use {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}} next.
* The turn after {{Int|Looter|Smoke Bomb}} has been used, it will {{Int|Looter|Escape}}.

=== In Party With ===

==== Act 1 ====
As a hard pool encounter:

* Solo

As half of the '''Exodium Thugs''' encounter along with either:

* 1 {{M|Red Louse}}
* 1 {{M|Green Louse}}
* 1 {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}
* 1 {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}

==== Act 2 ====
As an easy pool encounter along with:

* {{M|Mugger}}

== Mugger ==
{{Enemy Infobox|Mugger}}
{{Keyword Infobox|Thievery}}
'''Mugger''' is a normal [[Monsters|Enemy]] that can show up exclusively in [[Act 2]].

=== Pattern ===
{{Intents|Mugger}}
'''Mugger''' has the same pattern as '''Looter'''.

=== In Party With ===

==== Act 2 ====
As an easy pool encounter along with:

* {{M|Looter}}

{{Clear}}

== Trivia ==
* Looter appears in the Card art for {{C|Flurry of Blows}}.
* Mugger appears in the Card art for {{C|Clothesline}}.

== Update History ==
* Weekly Patch 36: Power Through
** Slaver/Looter and Slaver/Monster encounters in Act 1 swap positions to prevent Vulnerable + Attack turns.

* Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!
** Looter is moved from weak monster pool to regular monster pool (only appears after fighting 3 other 'weak' encounters on level 1)
** Looter + Mugger fight no longer allows you to steal back extra gold if you ran out of gold.
** Thievery Power now has correct name being applied to the Power.

* Weekly Patch 3: Balance Balance Balance
** Mugger doesn't give back gold it didn't steal

* Day 1 Patch
** Looter only refunds gold that was stolen now.
** Thievery power now displays how much gold is stolen per attack.

